# Everything here is consumed on Linux: shell scripts run through a shebang, cloud-init and
# user-data are pasted into a provider, and a CRLF in any of them fails with "bad interpreter"
# or a silently mis-parsed directive. Keep them LF whatever the checkout platform does.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
